{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1002026-does-the-technocracy-have-a-scp-foundation-equlivent","id":1002026,"title":"Does the Technocracy have a SCP Foundation equlivent?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-11T18:21:03-08:00","id":1002026,"title":"Does the Technocracy have a SCP Foundation equlivent?","content":"I was wondering that, what if there's Mages that the Technocracy cannot condition in Room 101 (which I wonder if this possible since the Technocracy can't be successful 100% of the time when they try to condition non-technocrat mages since I think there might be ones who either strongly believe or so far gone that is no point 'reasoning' with them so instead of conditioning them, they just contain them in cells), or they collect artifacts or even reality deviants that they call &quot;Anomalies&quot; (I was wondering if the Technocracy can use that term instead when describing supernaturals because they are Anomalous to their Paradigm) to put them into containment facilities for study which I wonder if the Technocracy could employ &quot;Class Ds&quot; (I wonder if it's possible for Technocrats to gnab Death Row prisoners for use) for testing.<br /> <br /> For example I could imagine the Technocracy containing really dangerous Maurderers and Nephandi in containment facilities to keep everyone safe from them and for testing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-11-2016, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:47:01-08:00","id":1002075,"title":"","content":"I don't know if something in this avenue was officially created, but for sure it is completely feasible, and a lot of people use this already.<br /> <br /> Something being immune to condition, or completely negated at some facility, it isn't so simple.<br /> <br /> Few things can be assumed as binary in Mage. As a rule of thumb, you can't rid a Major splat of its Supernatural Type, or kill the Sun or something of similar magnitude. Anything else is feasible. Nothing is automatic. And if one of those things isn't so relevant in your game, they're fair play, too.<br /> <br /> That means that ways to counter condition are perfectly feasible, if you guess correctly how condition will be done, and that condition is a magical work, and can be adapted to deal with any given way to counter it, if the conditioner can guess what protective means were used. The same goes on to any container facility, with procedures for containment being created trying to guess what means of counter-containment will be used to overcome them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T22:16:17-08:00","id":1002119,"title":"","content":"I suppose since it has never been brought up and it is your game. What I have always considered room 101 is from the TV show Babylon and Psi Corp and how they conditioned Mr Garibaldi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T09:46:10-08:00","id":1002255,"title":"","content":"The SCP Foundation is built off the idea that we shouldn't simply eliminate everything anomalous, but rather seek to make the world safe from it. They don't just throw everything into an incinerator. So the question is - would the Technocracy be more interested in containment or destruction?<br /> <br /> I'd argue destruction. The Technocracy (at least, the higher levels) knows why weird stuff exists - reality is malleable and there are lots of Reality Deviants able to alter it in various ways. Is there really a lot to learn from some Hermetic's talismans and books? If they're doing the Pogrom they'd want to follow leads to his colleagues, but they're not going to be mystified by a bound Umbrood in a pendant the way the Foundation is thrown for a loop by nearly everything it encounters.<br /> <br /> As for the Reality Deviants themselves, if they can't be converted, why would they be of any use? I can imagine a darker Technocracy that drains them of Quintessence first or downloads their mental state to a hard drive for later simulspace interrogation, but there's no upside in keeping a reality-warper that will always be working against you. It wastes resources that could be better spent elsewhere.<br /> <br /> If you really want the Foundation or something like it in your game, you can do a couple different things:<ul><li>Make the world weirder and/or the Technocracy less well-traveled. Maybe there are still plenty of Bygones out there, or legions of random Awakened not involved in the Ascension War and simply doing unique stuff. Or the Technocracy hasn't had nearly the history of success it's had in the books, and it's only now starting to understand vampires, werewolves, fae, etc. That gives your Technocracy a reason to want to know more about what it would find.</li> <li>Give the Technocracy a reason to never give up on conversion. Maybe they hold Reality Deviants in prisons where resonance fields slowly alter allegiances or change perceptions. Now it's worth it to maintain a prison, because you'll get a slow trickle of new Awakened recruits from it.</li> <li>Have reality be breaking down in a new and exciting way. The large-scale consensus is not as successful in homogenizing Earth as they might hope, and <i>things </i>come through the cracks. This puts the Technocracy in a position not of defining reality but of defending it from some sort of infection or decay that it doesn't understand - you'll get a reason for the research plus a good bit of desperation.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T10:38:47-08:00","id":1002263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1002026-does-the-technocracy-have-a-scp-foundation-equlivent?p=1002255#post1002255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SCP Foundation is built off the idea that we shouldn't simply eliminate everything anomalous, but rather seek to make the world safe from it. They don't just throw everything into an incinerator. So the question is - would the Technocracy be more interested in containment or destruction?<br /> <br /> I'd argue destruction. The Technocracy (at least, the higher levels) knows why weird stuff exists - reality is malleable and there are lots of Reality Deviants able to alter it in various ways. Is there really a lot to learn from some Hermetic's talismans and books? If they're doing the Pogrom they'd want to follow leads to his colleagues, but they're not going to be mystified by a bound Umbrood in a pendant the way the Foundation is thrown for a loop by nearly everything it encounters.<br /> <br /> As for the Reality Deviants themselves, if they can't be converted, why would they be of any use? I can imagine a darker Technocracy that drains them of Quintessence first or downloads their mental state to a hard drive for later simulspace interrogation, but there's no upside in keeping a reality-warper that will always be working against you. It wastes resources that could be better spent elsewhere.<br /> <br /> If you really want the Foundation or something like it in your game, you can do a couple different things:<ul><li>Make the world weirder and/or the Technocracy less well-traveled. Maybe there are still plenty of Bygones out there, or legions of random Awakened not involved in the Ascension War and simply doing unique stuff. Or the Technocracy hasn't had nearly the history of success it's had in the books, and it's only now starting to understand vampires, werewolves, fae, etc. That gives your Technocracy a reason to want to know more about what it would find.</li> <li>Give the Technocracy a reason to never give up on conversion. Maybe they hold Reality Deviants in prisons where resonance fields slowly alter allegiances or change perceptions. Now it's worth it to maintain a prison, because you'll get a slow trickle of new Awakened recruits from it.</li> <li>Have reality be breaking down in a new and exciting way. The large-scale consensus is not as successful in homogenizing Earth as they might hope, and <i>things </i>come through the cracks. This puts the Technocracy in a position not of defining reality but of defending it from some sort of infection or decay that it doesn't understand - you'll get a reason for the research plus a good bit of desperation.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>There is the point to consider not everything is made with sphere magic, Mage acknowledges that other supernaturals exist with their own forms of magic. If artifacts or creatures with such magic turns up, there is reason behind capturing them for study. It would be foolish for the technocracy not to capture a few specimens to understand how their magic works and if it can be used to benefit humanity.<br /> <br /> Mages are not all powerful and there are objects/creatures of power out there that give archmages pause. Mage are also limited by their paradigm and with how technocracy members depend on their foci(they can't overcome Any foci until arete 10, unlike tradition technomancers who can start at arete 6 or magic mages who start at arete 2), It's more likely only control even realizes they do magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:22:26-08:00","id":1002278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1002026-does-the-technocracy-have-a-scp-foundation-equlivent?p=1002263#post1002263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is the point to consider not everything is made with sphere magic, Mage acknowledges that other supernaturals exist with their own forms of magic. If artifacts or creatures with such magic turns up, there is reason behind capturing them for study. It would be foolish for the technocracy not to capture a few specimens to understand how their magic works and if it can be used to benefit humanity.<br /> <br /> Mages are not all powerful and there are objects/creatures of power out there that give archmages pause. Mage are also limited by their paradigm and with how technocracy members depend on their foci(they can't overcome Any foci until arete 10, unlike tradition technomancers who can start at arete 6 or magic mages who start at arete 2), It's more likely only control even realizes they do magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends how you view the Technocracy. To me, their goal is a safe, well-understood, well-ordered world. Keeping around things that are not well-understood and are certainly not part of the order they seek to create is counterproductive; if I want people to stop believing in dragons, why would I keep a dragon around for myself? Even if they find a phoenix whose tears cure disease - I get how the individual Technocrats might want it around, but the thing's existence and acceptance defeats the Technocracy's entire purpose. I would think Conditioning would force Technocrats to discard even those anomalies that would be personally beneficial, lest they be determined to be &quot;unmutual&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can take an alternate view in which the Technocracy isn't really advancing science but instead stealing. Maybe the Progenitors haven't devised a new, revolutionary medicine; maybe they just captured a whole lot of phoenixes and they show them sad movies all day in a big warehouse, with their tears collected by tubes and refined into the new wonderdrug. That's fine, and would even be kind of a cool world to play in, but isn't my thing. I prefer a Progenitor who'd say, &quot;Phoenix tears? Impossible. My heuristic RNA transferase, however...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T15:47:41-08:00","id":1002385,"title":"","content":"Technocrats who research Paradox would be the equivalent of the SCP Foundation, I'd say. Even if we assume that Technocrats suffer less Paradox, studying it heavily would still enable them to better manipulate, fight, and aid mystic Mages. An NWO who can manipulate a cabal into suffering Paradox Backlashes certainly doesn't need to call heavy firepower. A Progenitor could offer to neutralize Paradox Flaws, for a price. NWO and the Syndicate could help with Quiets. Trying to help a Mage - Technocrat or mystic - with a severe Quiet would be pretty SCPish. Likewise trying to free someone from a Paradox Realm.<br /> Technocrats who are fighting against Nephandi would especially benefit from wealth of knowledge about Paradox - in order to use it against Nephandi, and also to better work with any mystic allies they might have on their side.<br /> It could be a cross-Convention group within the Technocracy, consisting of few dedicated Amalgam who sometimes lend out single members to provide Paradox/Statistical Inevitability expertise where and when it's needed.<br /> <br /> Is it actually said anywhere how Paradox works for Technocrats exactly? Do they always get &quot;technocratic&quot; Paradox of machines blowing up, or can they actually end up in a Paradox Realm or have a Spirit sent after them, for using Inspired Science? I assume yes, but is it discussed or shown anywhere in the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-13-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:08:36-08:00","id":1002420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1002026-does-the-technocracy-have-a-scp-foundation-equlivent?p=1002278#post1002278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends how you view the Technocracy. To me, their goal is a safe, well-understood, well-ordered world. Keeping around things that are not well-understood and are certainly not part of the order they seek to create is counterproductive; if I want people to stop believing in dragons, why would I keep a dragon around for myself? Even if they find a phoenix whose tears cure disease - I get how the individual Technocrats might want it around, but the thing's existence and acceptance defeats the Technocracy's entire purpose. I would think Conditioning would force Technocrats to discard even those anomalies that would be personally beneficial, lest they be determined to be &quot;unmutual&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can take an alternate view in which the Technocracy isn't really advancing science but instead stealing. Maybe the Progenitors haven't devised a new, revolutionary medicine; maybe they just captured a whole lot of phoenixes and they show them sad movies all day in a big warehouse, with their tears collected by tubes and refined into the new wonderdrug. That's fine, and would even be kind of a cool world to play in, but isn't my thing. I prefer a Progenitor who'd say, &quot;Phoenix tears? Impossible. My heuristic RNA transferase, however...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that only works until the technocrats find themselves in a situation where they have no idea what they're being blasted with and their own plasma guns do nothing. If you don't understand what you're fighting you'll eventually find yourself in a situation you don't understand enough to fight back. I sort of see the techies capturing and studying things as absolutely necessary. Their paradigm is limited and completely relies on the scientific method of study to even function. So them not having a lab set up to hold, study, and possibly cure Anomalies/Reality Deviants seems counter intuative to their model of reality.<br /> <br /> I've never seen the technocracy as so much about &quot;order&quot; as understanding reality and using that understanding to make it safe for humanity. Blowing up every potential threat seems both counter-intuitive and destructive toward that goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T10:37:35-08:00","id":1002555,"title":"","content":"I think it might be a bit closer to what the SCP is if it was a separate organization from the Technocratic Union. An organization founded by mundane humans, who are ignorant of Consensual Reality and the larger Ascension War. They were just normal people, who saw weird things happening in the world, and vowed to contain what they see as threats to humanity. Kind of like the Arcanum, except instead of passively observing supernaturals, they act to bottle them up.<br /> <br /> Their only magical ability comes from captured items (Talismans, Fetishes, Charms, etc.), and from dedicated researchers studying captured items and creatures, as well as tomes plundered from occultists and the like. Sorcerers can be techno or mythic - indeed, they might mix and match whatever techniques they have available, simply because they are gathering such lore piecemeal. They have a couple scattered facilities devoted to research and containment, and fund themselves by deriving potential miracle products from materials captured. They wouldn't have access to unlimited Class D personnel, since they're probably not connected enough to make death row inmates disappear.<br /> <br /> Most probably, they've been infiltrated or courted by some members of the Technocracy, who seek to gain what they can from the Foundation's labs. The Syndicate might have reps who work with the Foundation (while pretending to just be interested business people, keeping the truth about the Union hidden), to help them bring their products to market. Indeed, they might serve in the same capacity that the SPD did - a place the Syndicate outsources its research and development work to - now that the latter disappeared mysteriously. And maybe the Union keeps an eye out for talented persons in the Foundation, snatching up the ones who seem likely to Awaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T20:56:30-08:00","id":1002759,"title":"","content":"Of course I also wonder how other <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/groups-of-interest\" target=\"_blank\">Groups of Interest</a> would fit in as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T16:23:33-08:00","id":1009077,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that the SCP Foundation is exactly the sort of thing that the VEs' Earth-based departments might involved with \u2014 a sort of inverse of the Syndicate's ties to the SPD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:44:07-08:00","id":1010234,"title":"","content":"Actually, a Foundation-esque covert &quot;contain and research&quot; facility on the part of the Technocracy is the setting for my current game. Of course, considering that the Agent in charge of the operation went Marauder, this isn't likely to be something the Union tries again any time soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T22:07:23-08:00","id":1011856,"title":"","content":"After reading this thread I delved in the Foundation-verse for 2 weeks straight, I think. Even distanced from the forum.<br /> <br /> That said, I did implemented a Foundation-esque institution on my current chronicle, but not within the Union. The idea of a mostly mortal Foundation appealed more to me in the end. They probably have some ties to supernatural institutions like the Technocracy, threading with them in the same way the Foundations does with GOI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}